  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted  therewith ( Application Form,  Flood Risk Assessment, 126/S/01, 126/S/02, 126/S/03, 126/S/04, 126/S/05, received 26/04/11.\r\nApplication letter, Design and Access Statement, Drawing Numbers 126/P/01A, 126/P/02B, 126/P/03A, 126/P/04B,  126/P/05B, 126/P/06A, 126/P/08, 126/P/09 received 04/07/11.)\r\nand approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - A scheme of sound insulation to protect the existing neighbouring residential dwellings from the proposed conversion and extension of the church meeting rooms and office into a church hall with ancillary facilities shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority prior to the proposed change of use taking place/ development commencing. The soundproofing shall be carried out in accordance with the approved scheme before the extended building is occupied.",
    "Condition : 4 - The extended building  hereby permitted shall not be used outside the following times: \r\n10am- 10.30pm Monday-Saturday, 10am - 4pm Sundays and Public Holidays\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 9:00am  to 5:00pm on Mondays to Friday and none shall take place on Saturdays, Sundays and Public Holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 6 - No deliveries shall be taken at or despatched from the site outside the hours of 8AM-4PM Mondays to Firdays, nor at any time on Sundays, Bank or Public Holidays.",
    "Condition : 7 - No development shall take place until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details",
    "Condition : 8 - The glazing formed in the balcony and window in the rearmost roof dormer shall be obscure glazed  and shall not be repaired or replaced otherwise than with obscured glazing."
